      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Tinker played a basic Mountain instead of Dormant Volcano. Dormant Volcano enters tapped and bounces an untapped Mountain, but it produces {C}{R} each turn - effectively ramping by providing 2 mana from one land. Since the player has Mycosynth Wellspring (2 mana), Tuktuk (3 mana), and Solemn Simulacrum (4 mana) to cast in upcoming turns, the extra mana from Dormant Volcano would accelerate their development. Playing Dormant Volcano now (bouncing the existing Mountain) means on turn 3 they can play the Mountain again untapped and have access to {C}{R} + {R} = 3 mana. Playing basic Mountain now means on turn 3 they'd have 2 Mountains for 2 mana, or play Dormant Volcano which enters tapped leaving them with just 1 Mountain untapped. Playing Dormant Volcano first is generally better for mana development since it gets the 'enters tapped' tempo loss out of the way early. However, Phyrexia's Core could also be considered since it provides colorless mana and has artifact sacrifice utility. The optimal play was likely Dormant Volcano to maximize mana on future turns.",
