    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Gem3F Tinker is discarding to Daretti's +2 ability (discard up to two, draw that many). They chose to discard Mountain over Dormant Volcano or Word of Seizing. Word of Seizing is a powerful instant that can steal any permanent at split second - it's much more situationally valuable than a basic Mountain. However, Dormant Volcano is also somewhat questionable to keep since it enters tapped and requires bouncing an untapped Mountain. The real question is whether keeping Dormant Volcano over a basic Mountain makes sense. Dormant Volcano taps for {C}{R} which is slightly better than a Mountain's {R}, but it enters tapped and bounces a Mountain. With 5 Mountains already on board (3 tapped, 2 untapped), a basic Mountain is arguably more useful as it doesn't cost tempo. That said, Dormant Volcano does produce 2 mana per tap which could be relevant for expensive spells. This is a close decision - discarding the basic Mountain is defensible but discarding Dormant Volcano might have been slightly better since the tempo loss of bouncing a Mountain is real.",
