      "better_line": "Cast Sphinx Summoner (3UB, easily castable with available mana) to get a 3/3 flyer and tutor an artifact creature, preserving all artifacts on board",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 261,
      "player": "GPT5n Drama",
      "decision_index": 393,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Sacrificed Cranial Plating instead of Blinkmoth Urn to Trash for Treasure. Cranial Plating synergizes strongly with Master of Etherium (the card being returned) and their artifact-heavy strategy. Blinkmoth Urn is symmetrical and benefits opponents (especially Gem3F Tinker with Wurmcoil Engine and multiple artifacts), making it the weakest artifact to keep.",
      "action_taken": "Sacrificed Cranial Plating to Trash for Treasure to return Master of Etherium",
      "better_line": "Sacrifice Blinkmoth Urn instead, keeping Cranial Plating to equip to Master of Etherium for a much more threatening board while denying opponents the symmetrical mana benefit",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 262,
      "player": "GPT5n Drama",
      "decision_index": 395,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "GPT5n Drama chose White from Fellwar Stone, but Plains already provides White mana. Choosing Blue would have enabled casting Sphinx Summoner (3UB) or Chief Engineer (1U), neither of which can be cast without a Blue source. With Blue from Fellwar Stone plus Rakdos Carnarium for Black, they could have cast Sphinx Summoner to tutor an artifact creature.",
      "action_taken": "Chose White from Fellwar Stone, which is redundant with the untapped Plains.",
      "better_line": "Choose Blue from Fellwar Stone to enable casting Sphinx Summoner (which tutors an artifact creature) or Chief Engineer this turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 264,
      "player": "GPT5n Drama",
      "decision_index": 398,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "GPT5n Drama cast Jor Kadeen, the Prevailer (5/4 first strike, gives +3/+0 with metalcraft if controlling 3+ artifacts) over Sphinx Summoner. Currently GPT5n controls only 2 artifacts (Fellwar Stone and Blinkmoth Urn), so Jor Kadeen's metalcraft is not active and he's just a 5/4 first striker. Sphinx Summoner (3/3 flyer) would tutor an artifact creature to hand, helping reach metalcraft and providing card advantage. Chief Engineer could also have been cast first to enable convoke for a bigger play. Additionally, casting a creature before combat (rather than after) when there's no immediate benefit gives opponents more information.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Jor Kadeen, the Prevailer without metalcraft active (only 2 artifacts on board).",
      "better_line": "Cast Sphinx Summoner to tutor an artifact creature (helping reach metalcraft threshold and providing a flying body and card advantage), or cast Chief Engineer first to enable convoke for future artifact spells.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 265,
      "player": "GPT5n Drama",
      "decision_index": 399,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Gem3F Tinker chose Daretti's -2 to sacrifice an artifact and return one from graveyard, but their only sacrificeable artifact appears to be Wurmcoil Engine (a 6/6 deathtouch lifelink). The graveyard targets are only Mycosynth Wellspring and Tuktuk the Explorer - neither worth trading a Wurmcoil Engine for. Even with Wurmcoil's death trigger creating two 3/3 tokens, this is a significant downgrade. Additionally, this costs Daretti 2 loyalty instead of gaining 2.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Daretti's -2 to sacrifice an artifact and return an artifact from graveyard to battlefield",
      "better_line": "Use Daretti's +2 to discard extra Mountains from hand and draw fresh cards, maintaining Daretti's loyalty and keeping Wurmcoil Engine on the battlefield.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 269,
      "player": "Gem3F Tinker",
      "decision_index": 409,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Tinker activated Loreseeker's Stone with 5 cards in hand (costing 8 mana) instead of first playing a Mountain from hand to reduce the hand size to 4 cards, which would have reduced the activation cost to 7 mana, saving 1 mana.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Loreseeker's Stone before playing a land, paying 8 mana with 5 cards in hand.",
      "better_line": "Play Mountain from hand first (reducing hand to 4 cards), then activate Loreseeker's Stone for only 7 mana, saving 1 mana that could be used for other purposes or kept available.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 271,
      "player": "Gem3F Tinker",
      "decision_index": 412,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Attacking with Goblin Welder for just 1 damage when it's a key utility creature. While GPT5n Drama has no blockers, keeping Goblin Welder untapped preserves the option to use its tap ability during opponents' turns to swap artifacts between battlefield and graveyard, which is especially relevant with Wurmcoil Engine on board and Pilgrim's Eye in the graveyard.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with all creatures including Goblin Welder for 1 extra damage",
      "better_line": "Attack with only Wurmcoil Engine and Solemn Simulacrum (8 damage), keeping Goblin Welder untapped for potential artifact swapping during opponents' turns",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 276,
