      "player": "GLM47 Philo",
      "decision_index": 440,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 12 life with two opponents active, GPT5n Drama passed on casting impactful spells. Sphinx Summoner (3UB) was castable using Fellwar Stone for U (via opponent's Exotic Orchard), providing a 3/3 flying blocker and tutoring an artifact creature. Trading Post was also castable for 4 mana, offering life gain and graveyard recursion. At low life, developing the board is critical.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to pass or take a non-spell action instead of casting available spells",
      "better_line": "Cast Sphinx Summoner to get a 3/3 flyer as a blocker and tutor for an artifact creature, or cast Trading Post for versatile defensive options including life gain",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 290,
      "player": "GPT5n Drama",
      "decision_index": 455,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "GPT5n Drama chose Red from Fellwar Stone when they already have abundant red mana sources (Mountain, Nomad Outpost, Rakdos Carnarium). They have Sphinx Summoner in hand costing {3}{U}{B}, and Blue was the one color they couldn't produce from any other source. Choosing Blue would have enabled casting Sphinx Summoner this turn, which tutors for an artifact creature - critical when at 12 life.",
      "action_taken": "Chose Red mana from Fellwar Stone",
      "better_line": "Choose Blue mana from Fellwar Stone to enable casting Sphinx Summoner ({3}{U}{B}), using Blue from Fellwar Stone, Black from Rakdos Carnarium or Nomad Outpost, and generic mana from remaining sources.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 290,
      "player": "GPT5n Drama",
      "decision_index": 455,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "At 12 life facing Wurmcoil Engine, GPT5n Drama tutored for Solemn Simulacrum (a value/ramp card) instead of a card that addresses the board state. Baleful Strix would be cheap to cast, provide a deathtouch flying blocker that trades favorably with Wurmcoil Engine, and draws a card. Ethersworn Adjudicator could directly destroy Wurmcoil Engine. Solemn Simulacrum doesn't help survive the immediate threats.",
      "action_taken": "Tutored for Solemn Simulacrum with Sphinx Summoner's ETB",
      "better_line": "Tutor for Baleful Strix (cheap deathtouch flyer to block Wurmcoil Engine + cantrip) or Ethersworn Adjudicator (direct creature removal)",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 292,
      "player": "GPT5n Drama",
      "decision_index": 456,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Tinker passed with 5 untapped mana and several useful plays available. Most notably, Ingot Chewer could destroy Blinkmoth Urn (which benefits opponents with artifacts) for just R via evoke, or Bottle Gnomes could be deployed as a 3-mana artifact creature providing board presence and a life buffer. Passing gives up free value.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting any spells despite having mana and reasonable options.",
      "better_line": "Cast Ingot Chewer (evoke for R) targeting Blinkmoth Urn to deny opponents artifact-based mana generation, or at minimum deploy Bottle Gnomes for 3 mana as a free artifact body.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 306,
      "player": "Gem3F Tinker",
      "decision_index": 485,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Gem3F Tinker has Wurmcoil Engine (6/6 deathtouch lifelink) and Tuktuk the Returned (5/5) plus Beetleback Chief (2/2) and two Goblin tokens (1/1 each) on the battlefield. GPT5n Drama is at 12 life with all lands tapped and no untapped blockers visible. Attacking with everything (6+5+2+1+1 = 15 damage) would be lethal against GPT5n Drama. Even just Wurmcoil Engine + Tuktuk the Returned = 11 damage, putting Drama to 1. GLM47 Philo is also at 34 life and all their permanents are tapped. There's no reason not to attack - skipping the attack phase entirely wastes a massive board advantage and misses a likely kill on GPT5n Drama.",
      "action_taken": "Skipped the attack phase entirely with a board of Wurmcoil Engine, Tuktuk the Returned, Beetleback Chief, and two Goblin tokens.",
      "better_line": "Attack GPT5n Drama with all creatures for lethal (15 damage vs 12 life), or at minimum attack with Wurmcoil Engine and Tuktuk the Returned to deal 11 and put Drama to 1 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 307,
      "player": "Gem3F Tinker",
      "decision_index": 485,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "GLM47 Philo activated Mosswort Bridge (which requires total creature power 10+ to play the exiled card, but they only have Dragonspeaker Shaman at power 2) instead of activating Bag of Tricks with Shamanic Revelation on the stack. Activating Bag of Tricks before Shamanic Revelation resolves could put a creature onto the battlefield, increasing the number of cards drawn from Shamanic Revelation and potentially triggering Ferocious.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Mosswort Bridge, which cannot meet its power 10 requirement with only a 2/2 creature.",
